{
  "info": {
    "name": "Delivez — Driver Assignment (ops)",
    "_postman_id": "0d4c3e7a-91f2-4b8e-a5d6-3c7f1e2b9a44",
    "description": "The ops console's **Driver assignment** screen as API calls: see deliveries waiting for a driver, pick a driver, assign, change and remove drivers.\n\n**Who can use it** (ADMIN-app login): FOUNDER, HEAD_OF_OPS, REGIONAL_HEAD, CITY_OPS and **driver assignment only** (role `DISPATCHER`) can assign. COMPLIANCE, FINANCE, LEGAL, SUPPORT and AUDITOR can only look.\nA login limited to some cities only sees those cities' deliveries and drivers. A delivery can only go to a driver of its own city.\n\n**Run it top to bottom.** Each request saves what the next needs (token, taskId, driverId…).\n1. Choose the **Production** environment, set `adminPhone` (10 digits, a console login).\n2. *1. Sign in* → **Send OTP**, put the SMS code in `otpCode`, **Verify OTP**. **Who am I** shows your role and cities.\n3. *2. Overview* → cities, counts, the waiting list. Set `orderNumber` to work on one order (e.g. DEL-123456); leave it empty to take the longest-waiting delivery.\n4. *3. Pick a driver* → the delivery, then its drivers, best first. Saves the first free driver as `driverId` and the next as `driver2Id`.\n5. *4. Assign* → assign, change driver (reassign), remove driver (unassign). Change and remove are allowed until the order is picked up.\n\nOptional variables: `cityId` (only this city), `orderNumber`. Errors: `{ \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\" } }` — e.g. 409 DRIVER_BUSY, 409 TASK_NOT_ASSIGNABLE, 403 CITY_NOT_ALLOWED, 400 VALIDATION_FAILED.\n\n⚠ Production: Send OTP sends a real SMS, and Assign / Reassign / Unassign change a real customer's delivery and notify the driver.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{adminToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "pm.request.url.query.each((q) => {",
          "  const m = /^{{(\\w+)}}$/.exec(q.value || '');",
          "  if (m && !(pm.environment.get(m[1]) || pm.collectionVariables.get(m[1]))) q.disabled = true;",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "requestId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "otpCode",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminRefreshToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "taskId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "driverId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "driver2Id",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Server",
      "description": "Is the API up?",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('database up', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().db).to.eql('up'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{$guid}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Sign in",
      "description": "OTP login to the ops console (app = ADMIN).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('requestId', j.requestId);",
                  "// Development / test servers only: the code is in the reply. On production it comes by SMS: put it in otpCode.",
                  "if (j.devCode) pm.collectionVariables.set('otpCode', j.devCode);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{$guid}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{adminPhone}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/otp/request",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "otp",
                "request"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Sends a 6-digit code by SMS to {{adminPhone}}. Saves requestId. Max 5 codes an hour."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify OTP (ADMIN)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('adminToken', j.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('adminRefreshToken', j.refreshToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{$guid}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"requestId\": \"{{requestId}}\",\n  \"code\": \"{{otpCode}}\",\n  \"app\": \"ADMIN\",\n  \"device\": {\n    \"platform\": \"web\",\n    \"app\": \"postman\",\n    \"deviceId\": \"{{deviceId}}\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/otp/verify",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "otp",
                "verify"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Put the SMS code in otpCode first. Saves the access and refresh tokens. 403 = this phone has no console access."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Who am I (role and cities)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json(); console.log(`role ${j.role} · ${j.allCities ? 'all cities' : j.cities.map((c) => c.name).join(', ')}`);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{$guid}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/admin/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "role (DISPATCHER = driver assignment only), cities, allCities."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json(); pm.collectionVariables.set('adminToken', j.accessToken); pm.collectionVariables.set('adminRefreshToken', j.refreshToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{$guid}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{adminRefreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "refresh"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Access tokens last 15 minutes. Returns a NEW pair; the old refresh token stops working."
          }
        }
      ]
